{
  "raw": {
    "https://collegeofidaho.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Dean-of-Students.pdf": {
      "title": "Dean of Students",
      "description": "                                                Posted: 9/30/2026                                        \n                                                Salary range: $92,993.00 - $103,326.00 \n                                      Status: Exempt, Full-time \n \nThe College of Idaho, invites applications for the position of Dean of Students, a vital senior \nadministrative role responsible for strategically shaping the holistic student experience outside \nthe classroom. Operating within a private, liberal arts framework, the Dean ensures that all student \naffairs initiatives align directly with the college’s core values, mission, and historic traditions. As a \nprimary advocate for student success, the Dean bridges the gap between academic rigor and co-\ncurricular life, cultivating a welcoming, safe, and vibrant campus community. \nIn this role, the Dean strategically oversees student engagement, campus life, and wellness while \nensuring a safe, supportive living and learning environment. Directing residence life, campus \nactivities, student organizations, outdoor programs, debate, campus ministry, and intercultural \ninitiatives, the Dean builds a welcoming and vibrant campus culture. In close collaboration with the \nAcademic Vice President and Deans of Undergraduate and Graduate Studies, the Dean designs \ncomprehensive orientation programs that foster early belonging and retention, while seamlessly \nblending classroom learning with student development. Additionally, the Dean partners with Health, \nWellness, Accessibility, and Learning Resources to support diverse student needs, while serving as \nan expert mediator for complex student-faculty disputes and academic appeals. \nFrom an operational and crisis response standpoint, the Dean leads the campus CARE Team in \nmanaging emergency interventions, threat assessments, and proactive mental health strategies. \nPartnering with institutional compliance, the Dean administers the student conduct code utilizing \nmodernized restorative justice practices and maintains rigorous adherence to federal regulations, \nincluding Title IX, FERPA, and the Clery Act. As a member of the President’s executive leadership \nteam, the Dean contributes to campus-wide policy development, acts as the primary liaison to \nstudent government, and manages departmental budgets to optimize student services. Through \nregular program assessments, data-driven retention tracking, and direct mentorship of student \naffairs staff, the Dean presents key metrics to the Board of Trustees to continually elevate \ninstitutional excellence. \nSuccessful candidates will possess a Master’s degree in Student Affairs, Higher Education, \nStudent Personnel, Counseling, or a closely related field, with a doctoral degree preferred. \nApplicants should bring five to seven years of progressive administrative experience within \nStudent Affairs, preferably in a private liberal arts college setting. This role requires a proven \nability to manage volatile campus issues under pressure, exceptional empathetic communication \nskills across diverse stakeholders, and deep expertise in higher education legal compliance, \nincluding Title IX and FERPA. Furthermore, the ideal candidate will demonstrate a strong track \nrecord in budget management, staff supervision, cross-cultural conflict resolution, and the \napplication of student development theory supported by proficiency in Microsoft Office and \nstudent information systems like Ellucian Colleague. \nCandidates must be authorized to work in the United States as of the expected hire date and \nthroughout the duration of their employment without sponsorship from The College of Idaho.  A \ncurrent, valid driver’s license is also required, and candidates must be vehicle-insurable. \nThe College offers competitive benefits, including tuition waiver for dependents, health insurance, \na retirement plan with employer match, generous paid time off, free access to on-campus fitness \ncenters, and free admission to campus events. Spouses, domestic partners, and dependents are \neligible for benefits coverage.  \n \n\nA complete application will include a current résumé, a cover letter addressing qualifications for \nthe position, and the names and contact information of three (3) references: two (2) from \nmanagement and one (1) professional, sent to careers@collegeofidaho.edu. Review of \napplications will begin immediately and continue until qualified candidates are selected. As we \nmove through the application review process, additional information may be requested from \nqualified candidates. \n \nWith over 134 years of history, The College of Idaho is a regional and national leader in higher \neducation. The College of Idaho is a mission-driven community of exceptional learning that \nchallenges the ambitious and forges pathways to success and purpose.  \n \nThe College of Idaho is proud to be an equal-opportunity employer. We are dedicated to attracting, \nretaining, and optimizing performance and academic excellence through an inclusive workforce. \nThe College does not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, religion, disability, national \nand ethnic origin, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other basis protected by \nlaw.  \n \n "
    },
    "https://collegeofidaho.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Events-Specialist-1.pdf": {
      "title": "Events Specialist",
      "description": " Posted: 08/06/2026 \nSalary Range: $35,568.00-$47,860.00\nStatus: Exempt, Full-time- Non-traditional hours \nThe College of Idaho is seeking an experienced, dynamic, detail-oriented Events Specialist to join \nthe Special Events and Conference Services team. In this pivotal role, you will coordinate and \nexecute a wide range of academic functions, campus initiatives, and signature institutional \nevents—including the Scholarship Gala, Go Purple, and Commencement—while also engaging \nexternal organizations to host events on campus to generate venue revenue. As a core operational \nliaison, the Events Specialist manages venue scheduling, delivers exceptional client service, and \noversees full event execution both on and off campus to support the College's vibrant community. \nThis role's primary responsibilities include collaborating with campus departments and external \npartners to schedule resources, conducting targeted outreach to maximize facility utilization, and \nmanaging specialized event software to generate timelines, room layouts, and invoices. You will \noversee operational logistics from initial setup through final teardown, troubleshoot basic \naudiovisual technology during functions, monitor event inventory, and administer billing, budget \ntracking, and utilization reports. Success in this role requires strong project management skills, \nexceptional written and verbal communication, proven problem-solving abilities under tight \ndeadlines, and the physical capability to walk, stand, and regularly lift up to 50 pounds during \nactive setups. \nThe ideal candidate will possess either a Bachelor's degree or a minimum of three years of \nexperience in event planning or hospitality, with a proven track record of successfully managing \nlogistics, timelines, budgets, and vendor negotiations. Essential requirements include proficiency \nin Microsoft Office Suite, hands-on experience with event management software, a valid driver’s \nlicense with an insurable driving record, and full availability to routinely work non-traditional \nhours, including mandatory evenings and weekends during peak event seasons and summer \nconferences. Preferred qualifications include prior experience in outside sales, business \nmarketing, and hands-on operational knowledge of presentation and audiovisual equipment. \nCandidates must be authorized to work in the United States as of the expected hire date and \nthroughout the date of their employment without sponsorship from The College of Idaho.  A \ncurrent, valid driver’s license is also required, and candidates must be vehicle insurable. \nThe College offers competitive benefits including tuition waiver for dependents, health insurance, a \nretirement plan with employer match, generous paid time off, free access to on-campus fitness \ncenters, and free admission to campus events. Spouses, domestic partners, and dependents are \neligible for benefits coverage.  \nA complete application will include a current résumé, a cover letter addressing qualifications for \nthe position, and the names and contact information of three (3) references: two (2) from \nmanagement and one (1) professional, sent to careers@collegeofidaho.edu. Review of \napplications will begin immediately and continue until qualified candidates are selected. As we \nmove through the application review process, additional information may be requested from \nqualified candidates. \nWith over 134 years of history, The College of Idaho is a regional and national leader in higher \neducation. The College of Idaho is a mission-driven community of exceptional learning that \nchallenges the ambitious and forges pathways to success and purpose.  \n\nThe College of Idaho is proud to be an equal-opportunity employer. We are dedicated to attracting, \nretaining, and optimizing performance and academic excellence through an inclusive workforce. \nThe College does not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, religion, disability, national \nand ethnic origin, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other basis protected by \nlaw.  "
    },
    "https://collegeofidaho.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Digital-Marketing-and-Social-Media-Coordinator.pdf": {
      "title": "Digital Marketing and Social Media Coordinato",
      "description": "                                                                                                           Posted: 09/02/2026 \n                                                Salary Range: $50,241.00- $55,824.00 \n                                                Status: Exempt, Full-time, On-site  \n       Non-traditional hours are required                                                       \n \n \nThe College of Idaho is seeking a dynamic and strategic Digital Marketing and Social Media \nCoordinator to elevate the college's online presence. This crucial role is all about sharing the inspiring \nstories and vibrant news of the college through its website, print materials, and social media \nchannels. The Coordinator collaborates closely with key campus stakeholders to plan, execute, and \nmonitor integrated campaigns that drive brand awareness, alumni engagement, and prospective \nstudent enrollment. This active and highly visible role requires a presence at campus events, athletic \ngames, and activities during standard business hours, as well as evenings and weekends, to capture \nauthentic moments in real time. \nThe Coordinator balances creative storytelling with strategic campaign management across multiple \ndigital platforms. Daily responsibilities include unearthing compelling campus stories, writing \nengaging web copy, and producing high-quality photo and video content, while also directing paid \nadvertising efforts on platforms like Facebook, Google, LinkedIn, TikTok, and YouTube. This involves \ntargeting the right audiences, mindfully managing ad budgets, and tracking performance. Success in \nthis role requires strong communication skills, a solid grasp of online advertising, and familiarity with \ntools like Google Analytics to optimize results. Being organized, self-motivated, and collaborative is \nessential for thriving in this fast-paced role. \nSuccessful candidates should possess a Bachelor’s degree in marketing, mass communications, \njournalism, or a related field, or have three to five years of equivalent professional experience. \nRequired qualifications include demonstrated experience leading social media strategy and content \nfor a professional brand, managing paid social and digital ad campaigns—including budget oversight \nand performance reporting—and utilizing content management systems (CMS) to create and update \ncontent across multiple channels. Candidates with prior success in an academic or comparable \ninstitutional setting, as well as hands-on experience with AI-assisted content creation and AI-driven \nadvertising tools, are strongly preferred. \nCandidates must be authorized to work in the United States as of the expected hire date and \nthroughout the date of their employment without sponsorship from The College of Idaho.  A current, \nvalid driver’s license is also required, and candidates must be vehicle-insurable. \n \nThe College offers competitive benefits, including tuition waiver for dependents, health insurance, a \nretirement plan with employer match, generous paid time off, free access to on-campus fitness \ncenters, and free admission to campus events. Spouses, domestic partners, and dependents are \neligible for benefits coverage.  \n \nA complete application will include a current résumé, a cover letter addressing qualifications for the \nposition, and the names and contact information of three (3) references: two (2) from management \nand one (1) professional, sent to careers@collegeofidaho.edu. Review of applications will begin \nimmediately and continue until qualified candidates are selected. As we move through the application \nreview process, additional information may be requested from qualified candidates. \n \nWith over 134 years of history, The College of Idaho is a regional and national leader in higher \neducation. The College of Idaho is a mission-driven community of exceptional learning that \nchallenges the ambitious and forges pathways to success and purpose.  \n \n\nThe College of Idaho is proud to be an equal-opportunity employer. We are dedicated to attracting, \nretaining, and optimizing performance and academic excellence through an inclusive workforce. The \nCollege does not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, religion, disability, national and \nethnic origin, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other basis protected by law.  \n "
    },
    "https://collegeofidaho.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Academic-Administrative-Assistant-.pdf": {
      "title": "Academic Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "                                                  Posted: 09/14/2026                                         \n                                                  Salary range:   $15.00-$15.66                                 \n                        Status: Non-Exempt, Full-time \n \nThe College of Idaho, is seeking an organized and customer-service-driven Academic \nAdministrative Assistant to provide crucial operational and administrative support across our \nEducation, Psychology, and Information Technology (IT) departments. Operating under general \nsupervision, this position serves as the welcoming face and central hub for assigned building \noperations, managing daily clerical activities and facilitating seamless communication across \nmultiple units. The ideal candidate will bridge academic programs with essential campus functions \nand frequently interface with key external entities, including the Idaho State Department of \nEducation. \nThis multifaceted administrative support position serves as the primary building receptionist and \nfront-office point of contact, greeting visitors, managing communications, and being an essential \nlink to the campus community. Core responsibilities include maintaining organizational calendars, \nscheduling venues, coordinating logistics and materials for special events, maintaining physical \nand electronic records, and assisting team members with travel arrangements and basic office \nequipment troubleshooting. On the financial side, this role monitors monthly unit budgets, \nreconciles corporate purchasing cards, verifies invoices for contracts and subscriptions, and \nmanages office inventory. Additionally, the role serves as a vital administrative contact to the Idaho \nState Department of Education, supervises student employees by preparing onboarding paperwork, \nand manages work schedules. \nQualified candidates must possess a High School Diploma or GED and at least one year of \nprevious experience in an administrative support or clerical role. Excellent oral and written \ncommunication skills, detail-oriented document control abilities, and proficiency in the Microsoft \nOffice suite (specifically Word and Excel) alongside basic database operations are essential. \nPreferred qualifications include prior experience handling basic budgeting, expense reporting, or \ninvoice reconciliation, as well as a helpful working knowledge of tracking required information for \nthe Idaho State Department of Education. \nCandidates must be authorized to work in the United States as of the expected hire date and \nthroughout the date of their employment without sponsorship from The College of Idaho.  A \ncurrent, valid driver’s license is also required, and candidates must be vehicle-insurable. \nThe College offers competitive benefits, including tuition waiver for dependents, health insurance, \na retirement plan with employer match, generous paid time off, free access to on-campus fitness \ncenters, and free admission to campus events. Spouses, domestic partners, and dependents are \neligible for benefits coverage.  \n \nA complete application will include a current résumé, a cover letter addressing qualifications for \nthe position, and the names and contact information of three (3) references: two (2) from \nmanagement and one (1) professional, sent to careers@collegeofidaho.edu. Review of \napplications will begin immediately and continue until qualified candidates are selected. As we \nmove through the application review process, additional information may be requested from \nqualified candidates. \n \nWith over 134 years of history, The College of Idaho is a regional and national leader in higher \neducation. The College of Idaho is a mission-driven community of exceptional learning that \nchallenges the ambitious and forges pathways to success and purpose.  \n \n\nThe College of Idaho is proud to be an equal-opportunity employer. We are dedicated to attracting, \nretaining, and optimizing performance and academic excellence through an inclusive workforce. \nThe College does not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, religion, disability, national \nand ethnic origin, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other basis protected by \nlaw.  \n "
    },
    "https://collegeofidaho.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/History-Berger-Neilsen-Endowed-Chair-of-Judaic-Studies.pdf": {
      "title": "History, Berger-Neilsen Endowed Chair of Judaic Studies",
      "description": " \n       Posted 9/10/2026 \n \n \nThe Department of History at The College of Idaho invites applications for an open-rank tenure-track \nappointment to the Berger-Neilsen Endowed Chair of Judaic Studies to begin in fall 2027. This position is the \nfirst endowed chair in Judaic Studies in the state of Idaho, and one of the few such chairs in the Pacific \nNorthwest and the intermountain region.   \nThe successful candidate will be a passionate, engaged teacher and productive scholar, who can provide \noutreach to the broader campus and local communities. The responsibilities of the Chair also include \nadministering the fully endowed Craig H. Neilsen Foundation Lectureship in Judaic Studies. Candidates must \nhave PhD in hand at the time of appointment in August 2027.   \nResearch specialization for this position is open, and applications are welcome from candidates \nwith expertise in the Middle East, Europe, and the Mediterranean. Preference will be given to candidates who \ncan offer engaging undergraduate courses on various topics of Jewish history and religion. Candidates will \nteach at least one course related to modern Israel and Palestine, broadly defined. The ideal candidate will be \nable to teach courses that would be accessible to a broad range of undergraduate students, most of whom \nhave little to no familiarity with Judaism.  The department values candidates with experience working with and \nmentoring students from diverse backgrounds. Approximately thirty percent of the students at The College of \nIdaho are first-generation college students; nine percent are international students representing fifty countries, \nand sixteen percent are Latinx.  \nCandidates must be authorized to work in the United States as of the expected hire date and throughout the \nterm of the contract without sponsorship from the College.  \nTo apply please send a cover letter, CV, recent course evaluations, and three letters of recommendation \nto careers@collegeofidaho.edu with subject line: Judaic Studies Search. Shortlisted candidates will be notified \nand asked to provide a writing sample. Letters of recommendation should be sent directly from referees or \nthrough Interfolio. Review of applications will begin on October 18, 2026, and continue until the position is \nfilled. \nWith over 134 years of history, The College of Idaho is a regional and national leader in higher education. The \nCollege of Idaho is a mission-driven community of exceptional learning that challenges the ambitious and \nforges pathways to success and purpose.  \nThe College of Idaho is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining, \nand optimizing performance and academic excellence through an inclusive workforce. The College does not \ndiscriminate based on sex, race, color, age, religion, disability, national and ethnic origin, veteran status, sexual \norientation, gender identity, or any other basis protected by law.  \nThe College offers competitive benefits, including a tuition waiver for dependents, health insurance, a \nretirement plan with employer match, free access to on-campus fitness centers, and free admission to campus \nevents. Spouses, domestic partners, and dependents are eligible for benefits coverage. \nThe College of Idaho is located in Caldwell, a rural community with a vibrant downtown that is on the western \nedge of the Boise metropolitan area, providing opportunities for both small-town and city living. The diverse \nlandscape of the area consists of river valleys, high desert, and mountains, which support a wide range of \nrecreational activities. Boise and the surrounding area also provide opportunities to enjoy a rich and wide array \nof cultural experiences and artistic venues. More information can be found at \nhttps://www.destinationcaldwell.com, https://visitboise.com, and https://visitidaho.org/. \n \n"
    },
    "https://collegeofidaho.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Chemistry-Visiting-Assistant-Professor-or-Lecturer.pdf": {
      "title": "Chemistry, Visiting Assistant Professor or Lecturer",
      "description": " \n       Posted 9/10/2026 \n \n \nThe Department of Chemistry at The College of Idaho invites applications for a full-time position to begin August \n2027. The position will be filled at the rank of either a Visiting Assistant Professor (1-year appointment) or as a \nLecturer (1-year appointme nt with possibility of renewal) , depending on the successful candidate’s area of \nexpertise and qualifications. The department is committed to delivering high-quality education and seeks \neducators who prioritize undergraduate teaching and mentorship.  \nA full-time appointment in this position will include teaching multiple lecture and laboratory courses during the \nfall and spring semesters as well as the possibility of working with more specialized courses during the college’s \nthree-week January term. Actual course assignments will be determined based on the candidate's experience \nand departmental needs. Special consideration will be given to applicants who can assist with instruction in one \nor more of the following lecture/lab combinations: Biochemistry, Analytical Chemistry, Forensic Science and the \nGeneral Chemistry I & II course sequence.  \nThe successful candidate will approach the undergraduate educ ation process with a growth mindset and a \ncommitment to collaboration with students in the course of their educational journey. \nCandidates should possess a terminal degree in chemistry or a closely related field, or an advanced degree in \nchemistry or bioch emistry and an appropriate combination of professional qualifications and certifications. \nCandidates who are ABD will be considered for this position.  \nCandidates must be authorized to work in the United States as of the expected hire date and throughout the term \nof the contract without sponsorship from the College.  \nReview of applications will commence immediately and continue until the position is filled. Please submit all \napplication materials to careers@collegeofidaho.edu with the subject line: Chemistry Search . Additional \ninformation may be requested from qualified candidates as we move through the applicant review process.  \nApplication packets should include: \n• A cover letter that addresses teaching inter ests and specifies which area , or areas , of the chemistry \ncurriculum the candidate is qualified to instruct  \n• Curriculum Vitae  \n• A statement of teaching philosophy that articulates a commitment to liberal arts education  \n• Evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., syllabi and teaching evaluations)  \n• Names and contact information for three professional references, with at least one reference able to \nspeak directly to the candidate's teaching  \nWith over 134 years of history, The College of Idaho is a regional and national leader in higher education. The \nCollege of Idaho is a mission-driven community of exceptional learning that challenges the ambitious and forges \npathways to success and purpose.  \nThe College of Idaho is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining, and \noptimizing performance and academic excellence through an inclusive workforce. The College does not \ndiscriminate based on sex, race, color, age, religion, disability, national and ethnic origin, veteran status, sexual \norientation, gender identity, or any other basis protected by law. \nThe College offers competitive benefits, including a tuition waiver for dependents, health insurance, a retirement \nplan with employer match, free access to on -campus fitness centers, and free admission to campus events. \nSpouses, domestic partners, and dependents are eligible for benefits coverage. \n\nThe College of Idaho is located in Caldwell, a rural communit y with a vibrant downtown that is on the western \nedge of the Boise metropolitan area, providing opportunities for both small -town and city living. The diverse \nlandscape of the area consists of river valleys, high desert, and mountains, which support a wide  range of \nrecreational activities. Boise and the surrounding area also provide opportunities to enjoy a rich and wide array \nof cultural experiences and artistic venues. More information can be found at \nhttps://www.destinationcaldwell.com, https://visitboise.com, and https://visitidaho.org/. \n \n "
    },
    "https://collegeofidaho.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Art-Assistant-Professor-Ceramics.pdf": {
      "title": "Art, Assistant Professor -Ceramics",
      "description": " \n       Posted 9/15/2026 \n \n \nThe Department of Art at the College of Idaho is seeking applications for a full-time, tenure-track position for \nan Assistant Professor of Art, specializing primarily in Ceramics. We are particularly interested in candidates \nwho see their specialization as a foundation rather than a limitation, allowing for broader engagement with the \nfield of art and design. The ideal candidate will possess substantial expertise in ceramics, along with the \ncuriosity, adaptability, and teaching range necessary to make meaningful contributions to our small, \ncollaborative department. \nThe College of Idaho is a liberal arts institution, and our Art Department serves students with a wide range of \ninterests and levels of experience. We are committed to providing students with opportunities to explore \nmultiple disciplines and approaches to creative practice, whether they intend to pursue art professionally, \nincorporate creative practice into another field, or develop a lifelong engagement with the arts.  \nThe successful candidate will teach introductory and advanced ceramics courses alongside foundations \ncourses focused on the elements and principles of art and design, while contributing to additional studio \nofferings based on departmental nee ds and personal qualifications. They are expected to maintain an active, \nfield-appropriate creative practice and develop engaging, rigorous coursework that welcomes non-majors while \nproviding depth for art majors and minors. Additionally, the candidate will fulfill all standard tenure-track faculty \nduties as outlined in the faculty handbook. \nRequired qualifications include an MFA or equivalent terminal degree in Ceramics, Studio Art, or a closely related \nfield by the time of appointment, along with demonstrated expertise and professional practice in ceramics and \ncollege-level teaching experience or potential for effective undergraduate instruction. Preference will be given to \ncandidates with experience teaching art foundations, 2D/3D design, drawing, digital  art, or related studio \ndisciplines, as well as additional expertise in art history or theory. Ideally, applicants will demonstrate experience \nworking across traditional and contemporary ceramic approaches, developing interdisciplinary or liberal -arts-\noriented curricula, and a strong commitment to teaching students from varied academic backgrounds and skill \nlevels. \nCandidates must be authorized to work in the United States as of the expected hire date and throughout the term \nof the contract without sponsorship from the College.  \nReview of applications will commence immediately and continue until the position is filled. Please submit all \napplication materials to careers@collegeofidaho.edu with the subject line: Art Search. Additional information \nmay be requested from qualified candidates as we move through the applicant review process.  \nA complete application packet will include: \n• A cover letter that addresses teaching interests  \n• Curriculum Vitae  \n• A statement of teaching philosophy that articulates a commitment to liberal arts education  \n• Evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., syllabi and teaching evaluations), and samples of student \nartistic work) \n• Work samples (still images, link to website, or media) \n• Names and contact information for three professional references, with at least one reference able to \nspeak directly to the candidate's teaching  \nWith over 134 years of history, The College of Idaho is a regional and national leader in higher education. The \nCollege of Idaho is a mission-driven community of exceptional learning that challenges the ambitious and forges \npathways to success and purpose.  \n\nThe College of Idaho is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining, and \noptimizing performance and academic excellence through an inclusive workforce. The College does not \ndiscriminate based on sex, race, color, age, religion, disability, national and ethnic origin, veteran status, sexual \norientation, gender identity, or any other basis protected by law. \nThe College offers competitive benefits, including a tuition waiver for dependents, health insurance, a retirement \nplan with employer match, free access to on -campus fitness centers, and free admission to campus events. \nSpouses, domestic partners, and dependents are eligible for benefits coverage. \nThe College of Idaho is located in Caldwell, a rural community with a vibrant downtown that is on the western \nedge of the Boise metropolitan area, providing opportunities for both small -town and city living. The diverse \nlandscape of the area consists of ri ver valleys, high desert, and mountains, which support a wide range of \nrecreational activities. Boise and the surrounding area also provide opportunities to enjoy a rich and wide array \nof cultural experiences and artistic venues. More information can be fo und at \nhttps://www.destinationcaldwell.com, https://visitboise.com, and https://visitidaho.org/. \n \n "
    },
    "https://collegeofidaho.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/General-Maintenance-Technician.-Full-time-Temp-to-hire.pdf": {
      "title": "General Maintenance Technician- Full-time, Temp-to-hire",
      "description": "                              \n                          Hourly Pay Rate: $20.00 - $21.00 \n                          Status: Full-time, Temporary \n                          Work Schedule: Mon – Fri  7 am – 4 pm \n         With the potential for On-call rotation   \n \nThe College of Idaho is looking for a dedicated and team-focused individual with excellent \ncustomer service skills to join our maintenance team! If you are dependable, detail-oriented, and \nhave the ability to troubleshoot, assess, evaluate, and address general maintenance and repairs, \nwe encourage you to apply and become a vital part of our campus community. This position is a \ntemp-to-hire opportunity, allowing you to demonstrate your skills and potentially secure a \npermanent role with us. \n \nTypical duties include:  \n• Performs general repairs that do not require a specialized technician- such as basic \nplumbing, routine electrical, carpentry, maintenance of building fixtures, and PM tasks.  \n• Manage assigned work orders through timely completion.  \n• Maintain a safe, clean, and organized working environment. \n• Ensure all hand tools, power tools, and equipment are maintained and in good working \norder. \n• Adhere to safety standards, operate a variety of gasoline, electrical, and diesel-powered \nequipment ranging from plows, scrapers, backhoes, skid steers, man-lifts, and related \nequipment. \nQualifications:  \n• Ability to successfully pass a criminal background check \n• Have strong communication skills in English, both spoken and written \n• Previous experience in a skilled maintenance position with similar responsibilities.  \n• High school diploma or GED, vocational or trade school a plus.  \n• Minimum 18 years of age \n• Possession of a current, valid driver’s license; vehicle insurable with a good driving \nrecord in accordance with The College of Idaho’s vehicle policy.  \n \nQualified candidates are encouraged to contact Elwood Staffing- Nampa, ID to share their resume, \nlearn more about the position, and the opportunity to interview.   \n \nEmployees of The College of Idaho are eligible for benefits including tuition waiver for dependents, \nhealth insurance, a retirement plan with employer match, generous paid time off, free access to on-\ncampus fitness centers, and free admission to campus events. Spouses, domestic partners, and \ndependents are eligible for benefits coverage.  \n \nWith over 134 years of history, The College of Idaho is a regional and national leader in higher \neducation. The College of Idaho is a mission-driven community of exceptional learning that \nchallenges the ambitious and forges pathways to success and purpose.  \n \nThe College of Idaho is proud to be an equal-opportunity employer. We are dedicated to attracting, \nretaining, and optimizing performance and academic excellence through an inclusive workforce. \nThe College does not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, religion, disability, national \nand ethnic origin, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other basis protected by \nlaw.  \n"
    },
    "https://collegeofidaho.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/HR-Data-Coordinator.pdf": {
      "title": "HR Data Coordinator",
      "description": "                                                  Posted: 10/15/2026                                         \n                                                  Salary range:   $20.71 - $23.01                                 \n                        Status: Non-Exempt, Full-time \n \n \nThe College of Idaho is seeking an organized and detail-oriented HR Data Coordinator to serve as \nthe primary gatekeeper for our human resources data. Operating under general supervision, this \nposition handles day-to-day data entry, auditing, and record maintenance within our Human \nResources Information Systems (HRIS). This is a foundational role focused on maintaining the \nintegrity, accuracy, and security of employee records. \n \nThis administrative support position plays a multi-faceted role in ensuring data integrity, delivering \naccurate reporting, and supporting core HR operational processes. Core responsibilities include \nentering and updating employee lifecycle data (such as new hires, terminations, compensation \nadjustments, and benefit changes), coordinating onboarding workflows, and running pre-payroll \nvalidation reports to identify and resolve data discrepancies before they impact paychecks. On the \ncompliance side, this role pulls standard compliance reports, assists the HR Director with \nspecialized regulatory reporting (such as IPEDs and 1095-C preparation), and maintains clear \ntechnical process documentation. Additionally, the role serves as a vital contact for student \nemployment, ensuring student hire paperwork is completed timely and accurately, verifying student \nwork eligibility, and entering/maintaining student employment data in our HRIS. \n \nQualified candidates must possess an Associate’s degree or an equivalent combination of \neducation and experience; a Bachelor's degree is preferred. One to two years of high-volume \nexperience in HRIS data entry or HR/payroll administration support is required; consideration may \nbe given to individuals with relatable skills from other fields. A high level of professional customer \nservice, strong organizational abilities, and a proven proficiency in the Microsoft Office suite \n(specifically Word, Excel, and Outlook) are essential. Candidates must demonstrate a solid comfort \nlevel in learning new technologies and software systems, alongside a high level of discretion \nrequired to handle sensitive or confidential information. \n \nCandidates must be authorized to work in the United States as of the expected hire date and \nthroughout the duration of their employment without sponsorship from The College of Idaho.  \n \nThe College offers competitive benefits, including tuition waiver for dependents, health insurance, \na retirement plan with employer match, generous paid time off, free access to on-campus fitness \ncenters, and free admission to campus events. Spouses, domestic partners, and dependents are \neligible for benefits coverage. \n \nA complete application will include a current résumé, a cover letter addressing qualifications for \nthe position, and the names and contact information of three (3) references: two (2) from \nmanagement and one (1) professional, sent to careers@collegeofidaho.edu. Review of \napplications will begin immediately and continue until qualified candidates are selected. As we \nmove through the application review process, additional information may be requested from \nqualified candidates. \n \nWith over 134 years of history, The College of Idaho is a regional and national leader in higher \neducation. The College of Idaho is a mission-driven community of exceptional learning that \nchallenges the ambitious and forges pathways to success and purpose.  \n \n\nThe College of Idaho is proud to be an equal-opportunity employer. We are dedicated to attracting, \nretaining, and optimizing performance and academic excellence through an inclusive workforce. \nThe College does not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, religion, disability, national \nand ethnic origin, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other basis protected by \nlaw.  \n "
    },
    "https://collegeofidaho.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Administrative-Assistant-Museum-Planetarium.pdf": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant -Museum &amp; Planetarium",
      "description": "                                                  Posted: 10/15/2026                                         \n                                                  Salary range:   $15.00-$15.66                                  \n        Status: Non-Exempt, Full-time \n                         \n \nThe College of Idaho, seeks a dedicated and organized full-time Administrative Assistant to \nprovide comprehensive administrative and operational support for the Orma J. Smith Museum of \nNatural History and the Whittenberger Planetarium. Under general supervision, this position serves \nas the primary point of contact for both facilities, providing professional, welcoming assistance to \nstudents, faculty, staff, visitors, groups, volunteers, and other external constituents. \nResponsibilities include managing front-desk reception, screening phone calls, responding to \nroutine inquiries, maintaining administrative records, preparing and proofreading documents, \ncoordinating office supplies, and managing building logistics in collaboration with Facilities. The \nposition also provides direct administrative and project support to the Museum and Planetarium \nDirectors. \nAdditional responsibilities include coordinating event reservations, meetings, and group visits; \nassisting with community outreach, monthly Museum Workdays, and special events; processing \nadmission, group visit, and event payments; and supporting Museum Gift Shop operations through \npoint-of-sale transactions, inventory monitoring, merchandise stocking, and ordering. The \nAdministrative Assistant also manages office and curatorial supply inventory, processes vendor \ninvoices, maintains accurate financial and administrative records, and supervises student \nemployees and volunteers. Occasional scheduled hours outside standard business operations may \nbe required to support events and special programming; these hours will be incorporated into  \nQualified candidates will possess a minimum of one year of experience in an administrative \nsupport, clerical, customer service, or related role. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications—\nparticularly Word and Excel—along with familiarity with basic database operations is required. \nCandidates with prior experience in budgeting, expense reporting, invoice processing, or financial \nreconciliation are strongly preferred. Furthermore, previous experience working within a museum, \neducational institution, cultural center, nonprofit organization, or visitor-service environment is \nhighly desirable. \nCandidates must be authorized to work in the United States as of the expected hire date and \nthroughout the date of their employment without sponsorship from The College of Idaho.  A \ncurrent, valid driver’s license is also required, and candidates must be vehicle-insurable. \nThe College offers competitive benefits, including tuition waiver for dependents, health insurance, \na retirement plan with employer match, generous paid time off, free access to on-campus fitness \ncenters, and free admission to campus events. Spouses, domestic partners, and dependents are \neligible for benefits coverage.  \n \nA complete application will include a current résumé, a cover letter addressing qualifications for \nthe position, and the names and contact information of three (3) references: two (2) from \nmanagement and one (1) professional, sent to careers@collegeofidaho.edu. Review of \napplications will begin immediately and continue until qualified candidates are selected. As we \nmove through the application review process, additional information may be requested from \nqualified candidates. \n \nWith over 134 years of history, The College of Idaho is a regional and national leader in higher \neducation. The College of Idaho is a mission-driven community of exceptional learning that \nchallenges the ambitious and forges pathways to success and purpose.  \n \n\nThe College of Idaho is proud to be an equal-opportunity employer. We are dedicated to attracting, \nretaining, and optimizing performance and academic excellence through an inclusive workforce. \nThe College does not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, age, religion, disability, national \nand ethnic origin, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other basis protected by \nlaw.  \n "
    }
